WEBVTT

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:08.610
Open your eyes. You'll get in an accident.

00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:13.630
Everyone's here.

00:00:14.710 --> 00:00:17.880
Today, we'll try running
to the river in Tamagawa.

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:19.680
I want to determine everyone's level,

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:21.750
so I can plan your practice
schedules for the future.

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:22.890
Keep that in mind.

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:26.900
There won't be a future.

00:00:28.950 --> 00:00:31.490
After all that, you're still participating.

00:00:33.330 --> 00:00:34.420
Just for today.

00:00:35.630 --> 00:00:38.600
You're some kind of freak, aren't you?

00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:41.820
Nothing beats eating after a run.

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:42.560
Let's go.

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:44.560
Wait.

00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:46.180
Wait!

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:49.270
Tamagawa? <i>That</i> Tamagawa?

00:00:49.270 --> 00:01:00.530
<b>Why</b>

00:00:49.630 --> 00:00:51.600
Yeah, that Tamagawa.

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:54.340
Isn't that five kilometers away?

00:00:54.340 --> 00:00:57.370
Wow! You're really familiar
with the local geography.

00:00:57.370 --> 00:00:58.140
Let's go.

00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:00.530
Wait, wait, wait!

00:01:00.530 --> 00:01:01.980
That's five kilometers.

00:01:01.980 --> 00:01:06.000
Five kilometers one way 
means ten kilometers round trip.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:07.580
Ten kilometers first thing in the morning?!

00:01:08.180 --> 00:01:11.420
If you can shout that much
after waking up, you'll make it.

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:12.540
Come on.

00:01:13.250 --> 00:01:14.860
What?

00:01:25.430 --> 00:01:26.600
He's fast.

00:01:28.930 --> 00:01:31.770
Start at your own pace.

00:01:31.770 --> 00:01:33.340
Come on. Go.

00:01:38.210 --> 00:01:40.200
Where is your dignity?

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:43.790
Where has your human dignity gone?

00:01:44.530 --> 00:01:48.340
We're allowing ourselves to be
forced to run without objection.

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:51.630
Can we really call ourselves people?

00:01:54.700 --> 00:01:55.890
Go.

00:03:23.090 --> 00:03:26.970
<b><i>Run with the Wind</i></b>

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:37.360
Yay. I won.

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:39.360
What? It was a tie.

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:41.620
I beat you by a hair.

00:03:49.930 --> 00:03:51.390
I'm impressed.

00:03:51.390 --> 00:03:55.610
This is the first time I've wanted
to go back to my home country.

00:04:08.610 --> 00:04:10.520
The theory will come later.

00:04:10.890 --> 00:04:15.400
First, your body needs to experience
firsthand how far five kilometers is.

00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:17.290
Then, you'll surely...

00:04:20.810 --> 00:04:23.400
B-Butterfly...

00:04:30.150 --> 00:04:32.580
You'll surely be able to run it.

00:04:40.720 --> 00:04:42.170
Okay, let's head back.

00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:45.680
What's wrong? Breakfast is waiting.

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:48.770
I'm going back as a butterfly.

00:04:48.770 --> 00:04:51.390
What are you talking about?
You're not making any sense.

00:04:53.370 --> 00:04:55.290
Hey, look.

00:04:55.290 --> 00:04:56.090
Huh?

00:04:56.680 --> 00:04:58.060
It's Kakeru.

00:04:58.060 --> 00:05:00.830
Is he ever going to stop running?

00:05:06.130 --> 00:05:08.770
Your body gets cold if you just wait.

00:05:09.810 --> 00:05:10.640
Yeah.

00:05:14.050 --> 00:05:18.730
Do you understand now 
just how stupid your idea is?

00:05:19.490 --> 00:05:22.520
They just ran a mere five kilometers.

00:05:22.520 --> 00:05:27.140
Every section of the Hakone
Ekiden is at least 20 kilometers.

00:05:27.140 --> 00:05:28.390
That's more than quadruple.

00:05:28.900 --> 00:05:34.270
We'll have to race that distance against
runners who have endured intense training.

00:05:38.180 --> 00:05:40.280
We could practice for 
ten years and still be behind.

00:05:44.590 --> 00:05:47.090
Just how insane is his body?

00:05:47.620 --> 00:05:48.770
He's not wrong.

00:05:50.330 --> 00:05:52.990
Don't worry. It won't take ten years.

00:05:53.770 --> 00:05:56.960
After all, there's less than
ten months until the race.

00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:04.420
<b><i>A Single Flower</i></b>

00:06:07.250 --> 00:06:10.610
At universities that participate
in the Hakone Ekiden,

00:06:10.610 --> 00:06:15.170
everyone runs 5,000 meters
in less than about 14:30 minutes.

00:06:15.590 --> 00:06:18.730
We'll consider that one of our goals.

00:06:18.990 --> 00:06:21.520
I have no idea what that looks like.

00:06:21.860 --> 00:06:24.950
The simple calculation is less
than three minutes per kilometer.

00:06:24.950 --> 00:06:26.040
What?!

00:06:26.040 --> 00:06:29.730
One kilometer in the time
it takes to prepare cup noodles?

00:06:29.730 --> 00:06:32.200
That makes it harder to understand.

00:06:32.830 --> 00:06:36.160
He means it's inhumanly fast.

00:06:36.500 --> 00:06:39.870
I bet there are lots of guys like
that where you're from, Musa.

00:06:40.140 --> 00:06:42.080
More prejudice.

00:06:42.530 --> 00:06:46.340
My high school's long distance
race was only three kilometers.

00:06:46.630 --> 00:06:49.470
Well, that's how it is.

00:06:49.470 --> 00:06:50.430
Thanks for the food.

00:06:50.930 --> 00:06:54.160
You're right that it's not 
an easy speed to achieve.

00:06:55.320 --> 00:06:58.060
But if you don't know what 
your goals are, you can't aim for them.

00:06:58.060 --> 00:07:00.180
Knowing's not enough.

00:07:01.480 --> 00:07:04.920
If you do the required training, it's different.

00:07:05.650 --> 00:07:08.030
We'll limit our focus to Hakone.

00:07:08.030 --> 00:07:10.400
That dramatically improves our chances.

00:07:11.580 --> 00:07:13.010
On what basis?

00:07:13.870 --> 00:07:17.240
On what basis are you making those claims?

00:07:18.140 --> 00:07:20.000
You don't want breakfast?

00:07:21.190 --> 00:07:22.990
I don't want to owe any favors.

00:07:28.710 --> 00:07:30.880
<b>Day 2</b>

00:07:41.020 --> 00:07:42.440
They ran.

00:07:42.950 --> 00:07:44.110
I'm going to wake them.

00:07:44.110 --> 00:07:45.900
Yuki never came home.

00:07:46.520 --> 00:07:47.290
Huh?

00:07:47.940 --> 00:07:49.960
He went clubbing as usual.

00:07:51.850 --> 00:07:53.850
Clubbing sounds nice.

00:07:53.850 --> 00:07:56.010
I bet there are lots of cute girls.

00:07:56.010 --> 00:07:58.160
We'll have to ask him to take us with him.

00:07:58.850 --> 00:08:00.270
Give me a minute.

00:08:01.220 --> 00:08:02.550
Huh? Hey!

00:08:03.250 --> 00:08:04.300
Kurahara!

00:08:33.670 --> 00:08:34.480
Whoa!

00:08:36.960 --> 00:08:37.660
Huh?

00:08:47.130 --> 00:08:48.380
Whoa...

00:08:48.380 --> 00:08:50.260
Haven't done that since grade school.

00:08:53.730 --> 00:08:57.010
Are you a Kansei Uni student?

00:08:57.010 --> 00:08:57.810
Yeah.

00:08:58.310 --> 00:08:59.880
On the Kansei Uni track and field team?

00:09:00.720 --> 00:09:02.040
Uh...

00:09:02.600 --> 00:09:03.480
Haiji.

00:09:04.210 --> 00:09:06.420
Are you familiar with Kiyose Haiji?

00:09:06.730 --> 00:09:07.590
Huh?

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:32.950
Hey!

00:09:34.290 --> 00:09:35.340
Hey.

00:09:35.610 --> 00:09:37.280
Haiji!

00:09:37.820 --> 00:09:39.700
What about school?

00:09:39.700 --> 00:09:40.770
After this.

00:09:40.770 --> 00:09:43.520
I came first thing, but no one was here.

00:09:43.520 --> 00:09:45.850
We're still slow.

00:09:45.850 --> 00:09:47.020
Who is that?

00:09:47.910 --> 00:09:50.480
I asked him if he was 
on the track and field team.

00:09:50.940 --> 00:09:53.020
I didn't see anyone else who could be.

00:09:53.020 --> 00:09:54.080
I was right.

00:09:54.880 --> 00:09:56.650
I couldn't ignore her.

00:10:03.670 --> 00:10:05.140
It's the Yaokatsu girl.

00:10:05.140 --> 00:10:05.930
What?

00:10:05.930 --> 00:10:09.790
Yaokatsu. She's the daughter of the
vegetable vendor in the shopping center.

00:10:09.790 --> 00:10:11.970
What? Are they dating?

00:10:11.970 --> 00:10:14.390
I doubt it.

00:10:14.390 --> 00:10:16.980
A high school girl's a little too young.

00:10:17.660 --> 00:10:19.340
Sorry. Let's get back to it.

00:10:20.060 --> 00:10:21.150
Guys.

00:10:22.100 --> 00:10:23.720
Practice hard.

00:10:26.150 --> 00:10:27.280
We will!

00:10:40.270 --> 00:10:42.740
Oh, wow! Then your future is secure.

00:10:42.740 --> 00:10:45.620
Really? I'll have to call you
for help if I'm ever on trial.

00:10:46.700 --> 00:10:48.580
I'd totally be down.

00:10:48.580 --> 00:10:50.540
You might be on trial?

00:10:50.540 --> 00:10:52.070
You never know.

00:10:52.460 --> 00:10:55.090
Can I get your number, then?

00:10:55.090 --> 00:10:58.050
It'd be hilarious if this were a scam.

00:10:58.420 --> 00:11:00.530
Of course it isn't.

00:11:00.530 --> 00:11:02.840
Then maybe I'll get your number, too.

00:11:02.840 --> 00:11:03.510
Huh?

00:11:08.300 --> 00:11:10.620
Are you crazy?!

00:11:11.860 --> 00:11:13.100
What?!

00:11:13.100 --> 00:11:14.490
Sorry. My ears.

00:11:14.860 --> 00:11:18.700
It's amazing. I don't know how
you can stay in there for so long.

00:11:18.700 --> 00:11:19.850
You're wasting your time!

00:11:19.850 --> 00:11:20.560
What?

00:11:20.560 --> 00:11:22.050
You're wasting your time!

00:11:22.050 --> 00:11:25.650
I don't have any reason to run
or anything to gain from it!

00:11:25.650 --> 00:11:28.830
I don't need to create memories
or network with you guys!

00:11:29.150 --> 00:11:34.530
This year of freedom
is my well-deserved reward!

00:11:34.530 --> 00:11:37.400
I deserve to savor this vacation from life!

00:11:37.400 --> 00:11:40.120
You're wasting your time
by trying to convince me!

00:11:40.120 --> 00:11:42.300
It's a total waste!

00:11:42.300 --> 00:11:44.590
I have a reason.

00:11:44.590 --> 00:11:47.600
I can't run in the Hakone
Ekiden without ten members.

00:11:48.210 --> 00:11:51.270
I don't exist for your purposes!

00:11:52.080 --> 00:11:53.100
You're right.

00:11:53.460 --> 00:11:58.100
Naturally, I don't intend to unilaterally
impose my will on you, Yuki.

00:11:58.620 --> 00:11:59.490
Then—

00:11:59.490 --> 00:12:00.400
I'll be back tomorrow.

00:12:00.400 --> 00:12:01.110
What?

00:12:01.110 --> 00:12:02.360
I'll come with you.

00:12:03.010 --> 00:12:06.120
After all, it's not fair to just
make you accompany me.

00:12:06.700 --> 00:12:11.860
It's very important for teammates
to respect and understand one another.

00:12:18.670 --> 00:12:21.670
<b>Day 3</b>

00:12:22.100 --> 00:12:25.140
Damn it. I'm finding a way out of this.

00:12:25.140 --> 00:12:26.640
Good morning.

00:12:30.200 --> 00:12:33.100
She's Yaokatsu's daughter,
 Katsuta Hanako.

00:12:33.100 --> 00:12:35.060
She'll be helping us sometimes.

00:12:35.320 --> 00:12:36.710
I've got school,

00:12:36.710 --> 00:12:40.130
so I can only help out early
in the morning and late at night.

00:12:40.130 --> 00:12:42.030
It's nice to meet you.

00:12:42.030 --> 00:12:43.540
Hey!

00:12:51.540 --> 00:12:53.500
<b>Why</b>

00:12:58.000 --> 00:13:00.870
It's a grand sight when everyone's here.

00:13:04.490 --> 00:13:05.560
Wait, Kurahara.

00:13:06.220 --> 00:13:09.450
I want to time everyone's finish. Help me.

00:13:09.450 --> 00:13:10.810
Why me?

00:13:16.140 --> 00:13:19.480
There's no need to go crazy
just because I'm timing you.

00:13:21.190 --> 00:13:24.750
I just want data to plan our practices.

00:13:27.930 --> 00:13:30.160
That's why I'm timing today's run.

00:13:33.250 --> 00:13:34.820
Don't hold back.

00:13:34.820 --> 00:13:38.240
I'll tell Hana to keep an eye out for that.

00:13:57.580 --> 00:14:00.890
Is that Haiji's girlfriend?

00:14:00.890 --> 00:14:02.690
The details are unclear.

00:14:02.690 --> 00:14:06.700
Being forced to run is already
a human rights violation,

00:14:06.700 --> 00:14:08.510
and now he's showing off his girlfriend?

00:14:08.510 --> 00:14:11.300
Just how much does he intend to toy with us?

00:14:11.300 --> 00:14:15.160
But it's clear now that King
has some hidden potential.

00:14:15.860 --> 00:14:17.640
It's sad, though.

00:14:17.640 --> 00:14:20.420
Yeah, no matter how you look at it.

00:14:29.350 --> 00:14:31.750
Well? I wasn't lying, was I?

00:14:32.500 --> 00:14:33.500
About what?

00:14:34.690 --> 00:14:35.740
The girl.

00:14:37.650 --> 00:14:41.350
Work hard, and women will approach you.

00:14:41.910 --> 00:14:43.780
It only took three days.

00:14:43.780 --> 00:14:47.860
If you keep getting stronger
and attract more attention...

00:14:51.330 --> 00:14:53.950
Haiji, we're sorry.

00:14:54.330 --> 00:14:57.130
We doubted you.

00:14:57.130 --> 00:15:01.750
We thought you were tricking us.

00:15:03.780 --> 00:15:06.010
But it was true!

00:15:06.010 --> 00:15:11.970
It's only Yaokatsu's Hana so far,
but as long as we work hard...

00:15:11.970 --> 00:15:14.070
That's right. Look!

00:15:15.950 --> 00:15:20.180
On the other side of the road
are more women than you can count!

00:15:21.980 --> 00:15:23.730
I'm so glad...

00:15:23.730 --> 00:15:25.640
We decided to attend college...

00:15:29.190 --> 00:15:30.750
They've been fooled.

00:15:30.750 --> 00:15:32.680
They sure have.

00:15:32.680 --> 00:15:35.920
Okay! Let's aim for the top!

00:15:36.340 --> 00:15:38.540
What? What if we actually win?

00:15:38.540 --> 00:15:40.000
Well, my boy...

00:15:40.510 --> 00:15:41.710
You'll have your hands full.

00:15:43.230 --> 00:15:45.830
The mountains of Hakone
are the steepest in the world!

00:15:45.830 --> 00:15:48.340
I don't know what that means!

00:15:48.340 --> 00:15:50.670
But it's so intense!

00:15:50.670 --> 00:15:51.980
The mountains of Hakone are?

00:15:51.980 --> 00:15:53.340
The steepest in the world!

00:15:53.340 --> 00:15:54.790
The mountains of Hakone are?

00:15:54.790 --> 00:15:55.960
The steepest in the world!

00:15:55.090 --> 00:15:55.940
Musa.

00:15:55.940 --> 00:15:56.850
What?

00:15:57.740 --> 00:16:00.800
I'm thinking about continuing a while longer.

00:16:01.620 --> 00:16:02.460
Huh?

00:16:03.020 --> 00:16:05.600
How dare they be fooled so easily?!

00:16:06.390 --> 00:16:09.730
What about you? I thought you
were going to make him give up.

00:16:10.270 --> 00:16:12.540
Don't tell me you're on board now.

00:16:13.110 --> 00:16:14.200
Yeah, right.

00:16:14.450 --> 00:16:22.160
<b>Why</b>

00:16:14.790 --> 00:16:18.590
Prince can't even finish properly.

00:16:18.590 --> 00:16:21.610
No one would believe him.

00:16:24.190 --> 00:16:25.920
Right.

00:16:26.670 --> 00:16:29.840
So why is he so confident?

00:16:33.200 --> 00:16:35.760
Let's head back! Time for breakfast!

00:16:46.650 --> 00:16:48.610
<b>Yaokatsu</b>

00:16:47.960 --> 00:16:50.280
Did I do good this morning?

00:16:50.280 --> 00:16:51.900
Yeah, it was plenty.

00:16:52.330 --> 00:16:56.140
Athletes perform better
in front of an audience.

00:16:56.920 --> 00:17:00.450
Huh. It really was fun, though.

00:17:00.830 --> 00:17:01.950
That's good.

00:17:02.490 --> 00:17:04.910
It's effective, even if all
you're doing is watching.

00:17:05.290 --> 00:17:07.920
I hope your dream comes true.

00:17:07.920 --> 00:17:09.180
It will.

00:17:09.180 --> 00:17:09.880
Huh?

00:17:10.140 --> 00:17:11.950
He's been waiting four years.

00:17:11.950 --> 00:17:13.880
You've got some good members, right?

00:17:13.880 --> 00:17:17.300
I heard she couldn't keep up on her bike.

00:17:17.300 --> 00:17:19.820
Yeah. He was amazing.

00:17:20.240 --> 00:17:22.560
Is Kurahara famous?

00:17:23.160 --> 00:17:25.060
I'm not sure.

00:17:25.060 --> 00:17:27.320
Either way, I'm excited.

00:17:27.320 --> 00:17:32.030
Let me know if there's
anything we can do to help.

00:17:32.300 --> 00:17:33.640
Thank you.

00:17:34.990 --> 00:17:37.490
<b>Tsuru-no-yu</b>

00:17:38.230 --> 00:17:40.390
What? Qualifier?

00:17:40.390 --> 00:17:41.910
Joji, your bubbles.

00:17:42.380 --> 00:17:46.360
Most people only know about the actual race.

00:17:48.100 --> 00:17:50.110
I just learned about it today.

00:17:50.110 --> 00:17:53.060
Of the twenty schools that participate
in the Hakone Ekiden,

00:17:53.060 --> 00:17:56.830
aside from the ten seeded teams
that qualify the previous year,

00:17:56.830 --> 00:18:01.350
they have to participate
in a preliminary qualifier.

00:18:01.660 --> 00:18:02.960
Really?

00:18:04.410 --> 00:18:07.360
Then we'll race in that first.

00:18:07.360 --> 00:18:08.350
All right!

00:18:09.030 --> 00:18:11.770
We still don't know if we'll be racing.

00:18:13.260 --> 00:18:16.590
How many schools participate in the qualifier?

00:18:16.590 --> 00:18:19.020
About fifty.

00:18:19.020 --> 00:18:21.550
So only the top fifth qualify.

00:18:21.550 --> 00:18:23.110
I bet we can do it if we try.

00:18:23.110 --> 00:18:26.440
Yeah. Haiji said we're just getting started.

00:18:26.440 --> 00:18:30.190
We can do it as long as we practice hard.

00:18:30.190 --> 00:18:31.440
It's not that easy.

00:18:34.140 --> 00:18:39.590
How hard do you think they
practice to be in the top fifth?

00:18:40.200 --> 00:18:43.850
And not everyone can
participate in the qualifier.

00:18:44.350 --> 00:18:48.900
Each athlete needs an official record
of finishing 5,000 meters in less than 16:30

00:18:48.900 --> 00:18:52.190
or 10,000 in 30:00.

00:18:54.460 --> 00:18:56.730
Those are astronomical figures.

00:18:56.730 --> 00:19:00.740
You have to achieve those
records before the qualifier.

00:19:01.530 --> 00:19:04.330
It doesn't matter if you have
a couple of fast guys.

00:19:04.770 --> 00:19:07.280
Everyone has to be running at a high level.

00:19:08.790 --> 00:19:13.630
An amateur who can't even finish
ten kilometers shouldn't be aiming for that.

00:19:13.990 --> 00:19:18.100
Don't you understand how reckless he's being?

00:19:19.230 --> 00:19:21.020
Kinda.

00:19:21.020 --> 00:19:22.950
Then stop wasting your efforts.

00:19:22.950 --> 00:19:23.760
Actually,

00:19:24.280 --> 00:19:26.260
What's your deal, Kakeru?

00:19:26.260 --> 00:19:27.320
What?

00:19:28.020 --> 00:19:30.990
Yeah. What are you afraid of?

00:19:30.990 --> 00:19:32.060
You're fast.

00:19:32.060 --> 00:19:33.000
What?!

00:19:33.420 --> 00:19:36.130
Maybe you're worried about us,

00:19:36.130 --> 00:19:38.190
but we're the ones doing the work, so who cares?

00:19:39.030 --> 00:19:40.950
Run with us.

00:19:47.960 --> 00:19:53.200
I don't work well with others.

00:20:11.520 --> 00:20:12.820
Where's Kurahara?

00:20:12.820 --> 00:20:14.560
He left already.

00:20:14.560 --> 00:20:17.640
We only ran together for one day.

00:20:17.640 --> 00:20:19.530
Maybe he's mad.

00:20:36.610 --> 00:20:38.480
Run with us.

00:20:41.420 --> 00:20:42.870
I knew it.

00:20:53.120 --> 00:20:56.190
It's been a while, Kurahara.

00:22:40.650 --> 00:22:42.970
Next time: "Shadows That Don't Fade."

00:22:40.670 --> 00:22:45.510
<b>Next Time: Shadows That Don't Fade</b>
